    {
      "status": "fill",
      "field": {
        "id": "265166de-3b04-4ec6-84e0-0ca7203a9980",
        "label": "Please describe your AI experience.",
        "kind": "textarea",
        "required": true,
        "options": []
      },
      "value": "My AI experience spans applied ML research, computer vision systems, and LLM-based prototypes, which maps well to Notion’s focus on model-powered features, retrieval/orchestration, and eval loops. At Arborphy AI, I work on plant identification models, including an EfficientNet–BioCLIP dual-encoder with cross-attention, and I run controlled fusion, retrieval, and held-out evaluations to understand when model changes actually improve recognition. I also built a multi-agent botanical reasoning prototype with tool generation, iterative planning, and knowledge-graph evidence aggregation. Previously, I built a real-time robotics vision pipeline with YOLOv8, pose estimation, stereo tracking, and ONNX Runtime optimization, and integrated a locally hosted language model through Ollama for voice-based robot commands. I’ve also studied hallucination mechanisms in Qwen models using activation hooks, probes, and steering controls.",
      "source": {
        "type": "bank",
        "id": "draft:13967e1c35",
        "origin": "generated"
      },
      "confidence": 1,
      "sensitive": false
    },
    {
      "status": "fill",
      "field": {
        "id": "1dab9be1-ccb6-4584-96fe-574bbffeb9a9",
        "label": "What are some AI specific technologies you are comfortable with?",
        "kind": "textarea",
        "required": true,
        "options": []
      },
      "value": "I’m comfortable working in Python with PyTorch, Hugging Face, scikit-learn, and vLLM. On the model side, I’ve worked with LLMs and transformer tooling, including Qwen3, TransformerLens, activation hooks, linear probes, steering scripts, and Hugging Face consistency checks. I’ve also integrated a locally hosted language model through Ollama for voice-based robot commands. For vision and ML systems, I’ve used EfficientNet, BioCLIP, DINOv3, YOLOv8, ResNet, U-Net, ONNX Runtime, quantization, and retrieval-style benchmarks. I’ve built evaluation loops with multi-seed experiments, grouped held-out evaluations, ablations, and controlled known-versus-unknown prompt experiments, which maps well to Notion’s focus on LLM-powered features and evals.",
      "source": {
        "type": "bank",
        "id": "draft:bf535e461e",
        "origin": "generated"
      },
      "confidence": 1,
      "sensitive": false
    },
    {
      "status": "fill",
      "field": {
        "id": "4b31a0ec-c052-4046-84c1-acb10812ec01",
        "label": "Why do you want to work at Notion?",
        "kind": "textarea",
        "required": true,
        "options": []
      },
      "value": "I want to work at Notion because this role treats AI as part of a real working product: UX, APIs, retrieval, orchestration, quality, reliability, and evals, rather than as a model demo. That matches how I like to build. I’ve integrated a locally hosted language model into a robot control workflow, built a multi-agent botanical reasoning prototype with tool generation and evidence aggregation, and run careful controlled experiments to understand when an architecture actually improves outcomes. I’m especially drawn to Notion’s focus on helping people work with less fragmentation. My research and engineering work has often been about turning complex ML systems into usable pipelines, tools, and documentation for other people, and I’d like to do that at product scale.",
      "source": {
        "type": "bank",
        "id": "draft:64ba8f323d",
        "origin": "generated"
      },
      "confidence": 1,
      "sensitive": false
    },
